{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.03 | Right-click to rename the window title or save filename. Turns cyan when there are unsaved changes. Use ≡ to toggle Hierarchy, </> for Source, ▶ Preview for live data, ⊟ for the Properties panel.\nPalette (auto-hide) | 0.02, 0.50 | Move the mouse to the far left edge to reveal ~50 WPF controls grouped into Layout, Controls, Data, Shapes, Media, and Menus. Drag any tile onto the canvas to insert it as a new element.\nHierarchy Panel | 0.11, 0.42 | Tree view of every XAML element. Click to select, ▶/▼ to expand or collapse, · marks leaf nodes. Drag rows to reorder. Label shows type (teal) then x:Name, Content, or text hint (grey).\nCanvas | 0.40, 0.42 | Click an element to select it (8-handle frame appears). Drag to move (Canvas.Left/Top). Drag a corner or edge handle to resize. Ctrl+C/X/V/D copy/cut/paste/duplicate. Delete removes. Shift+scroll pans horizontally.\nSource Panel | 0.40, 0.77 | Syntax-highlighted XAML source. Click a row to select that element. Drag rows to reorder elements. Teal=element names, Cyan=attribute names, Orange=values, Yellow=x: attrs, Green=comments.\nProperties | 0.83, 0.30 | All attributes of the selected element. Edit values directly (Enter or click away to apply). Click a colour swatch to open the colour picker. Cyan { } pills are data-binding expressions — click ✏ to edit. + Add Attribute adds new rows; × deletes them.\nData Context | 0.83, 0.65 | Define a JSON ViewModel and NCalc computed expressions. Click Apply to parse. Click ▶ Preview in the title bar to resolve all {Binding Path} expressions on the canvas to real values. FallbackValue and StringFormat are supported.\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: AIDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}